{"task_id": "Mbpp/104", "solution": "def sort_sublists(lists):\n    \"\"\"\n    Sort each sublist of strings in the given iterable of iterables.\n    Returns a new list of lists with each inner list sorted lexicographically.\n    Raises TypeError if the outer input is not iterable, a sublist is not iterable,\n    or any item in a sublist is not a string.\n    \"\"\"\n    try:\n        iter(lists)\n    except TypeError:\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be an iterable of iterables.\")\n\n    sorted_outer = []\n    for i, sub in enumerate(lists):\n        try:\n            sub_list = list(sub)\n        except TypeError:\n            raise TypeError(f\"Sublist at index {i} is not iterable.\")\n        for j, item in enumerate(sub_list):\n            if not isinstance(item, str):\n                raise TypeError(f\"Item at index [{i}][{j}] is not a string.\")\n        sorted_outer.append(sorted(sub_list))\n    return sorted_outer"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/103", "solution": "def eulerian_num(n: int, m: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the Eulerian number a(n, m) using an iterative dynamic programming approach.\n    It follows the recurrence relation A(n,m) = (n-m)*A(n-1,m-1) + (m+1)*A(n-1,m).\n    \"\"\"\n    # Validate inputs\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or not isinstance(m, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"n and m must be integers\")\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"n must be >= 0\")\n    if n == 0 and m == 0:\n        return 1\n    if m < 0 or m >= n:\n        return 0\n\n    # Initialize the 'previous' row for DP: A(0,0)=1, others 0.\n    prev = [0] * (n if n > 0 else 1)\n    prev[0] = 1\n\n    # Build rows from i = 1 .. n\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        # A(i, k) valid for 0 <= k < i; allocate i+1 to simplify indexing\n        cur = [0] * (i + 1)\n        for j in range(i):\n            term1 = (i - j) * (prev[j - 1] if j - 1 >= 0 and j - 1 < len(prev) else 0)\n            term2 = (j + 1) * (prev[j] if j < len(prev) else 0)\n            cur[j] = term1 + term2\n        prev = cur\n\n    return prev[m]"}
