{"task_id": "Mbpp/232", "solution": "def larg_nnum(lst, n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns a list containing the n largest unique items from the input list, sorted in descending order.\n    Handles non-positive n by returning an empty list.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 0:\n        return []\n\n    # Get unique elements and sort them in descending order\n    unique_sorted_items = sorted(list(set(lst)), reverse=True)\n\n    # Return the first n elements\n    return unique_sorted_items[:n]"}
