{"task_id": "Mbpp/235", "solution": "def even_bit_set_number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sets all even 1-indexed bits of a given non-negative number to 1.\n    The mask covers even positions up to the smallest even index >= n's bit_length (minimum 2).\n    \"\"\"\n    # Determine the effective bit length for the mask.\n    # n.bit_length() returns 0 for n=0, 1 for n=1, etc.\n    bit_len = n.bit_length()\n\n    # Calculate the mask length: smallest even number greater than or equal to bit_len,\n    # with a minimum of 2 bits.\n    if bit_len == 0:\n        mask_len = 2\n    elif bit_len % 2 == 0:\n        mask_len = bit_len\n    else:\n        mask_len = bit_len + 1\n\n    mask = 0\n    # Iterate through 1-indexed even bit positions (2, 4, 6, ...) up to mask_len.\n    # The actual bit index for the bitwise operation is (position - 1).\n    for pos in range(2, mask_len + 1, 2):\n        mask |= (1 << (pos - 1))\n\n    # Apply the mask using a bitwise OR operation.\n    return n | mask"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/238", "solution": "def number_of_substrings(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of non-empty substrings in a given string.\n    This includes substrings at different positions, even if their content is identical.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(s)\n    # The number of substrings is the sum of lengths from 1 to n: n + (n-1) + ... + 1\n    # This sum can be calculated with the formula n * (n + 1) / 2.\n    # Using integer division // 2 ensures an integer result.\n    return n * (n + 1) // 2"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/237", "solution": "def check_occurences(tuple_list):\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts occurrences of canonicalized tuples in a list.\n    Tuples are canonicalized by sorting their elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    counts = {}\n    for t in tuple_list:\n        # Canonicalize the tuple by sorting its elements\n        canonical_tuple = tuple(sorted(t))\n        counts[canonical_tuple] = counts.get(canonical_tuple, 0) + 1\n    return counts"}
