{"task_id": "Mbpp/247", "solution": "def lps(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the length of the longest palindromic subsequence of the given string.\n    Uses dynamic programming with O(N^2) time and space complexity.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(s)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # dp[i][j] stores the length of the longest palindromic subsequence\n    # for the substring s[i...j]\n    dp = [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # All single characters are palindromes of length 1\n    for i in range(n):\n        dp[i][i] = 1\n\n    # Fill the DP table for lengths from 2 to n\n    for length in range(2, n + 1):\n        for i in range(n - length + 1):\n            j = i + length - 1\n            if s[i] == s[j]:\n                # If characters match, add 2 to the LPS of the inner substring\n                # Handle case when inner substring is empty (i+1 > j-1)\n                if i + 1 <= j - 1:\n                    dp[i][j] = dp[i + 1][j - 1] + 2\n                else:\n                    dp[i][j] = 2\n            else:\n                # If characters don't match, take the maximum of excluding s[i] or s[j]\n                dp[i][j] = max(dp[i + 1][j], dp[i][j - 1])\n\n    return dp[0][n - 1]"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/245", "solution": "from typing import Sequence\ndef max_sum(arr: Sequence[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum sum of a bitonic subsequence for the given array.\n    A sequence is bitonic if it is first strictly increasing and then strictly decreasing.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not arr:\n        return 0\n\n    n = len(arr)\n\n    # inc[i] stores the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence ending at arr[i]\n    inc = [0] * n\n    for i in range(n):\n        inc[i] = arr[i]\n        for j in range(i):\n            if arr[j] < arr[i] and inc[j] + arr[i] > inc[i]:\n                inc[i] = inc[j] + arr[i]\n\n    # dec[i] stores the maximum sum of a decreasing subsequence starting at arr[i]\n    dec = [0] * n\n    for i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):\n        dec[i] = arr[i]\n        for j in range(n - 1, i, -1):\n            if arr[j] < arr[i] and dec[j] + arr[i] > dec[i]:\n                dec[i] = dec[j] + arr[i]\n\n    # Combine increasing and decreasing sums, subtracting arr[i] as it's counted twice.\n    return max(inc[i] + dec[i] - arr[i] for i in range(n))"}
