{"task_id": "Mbpp/721", "solution": "def maxAverageOfPath(matrix):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum average cost of a path from the top-left to the bottom-right cell\n    in a square matrix, moving only right or down.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(matrix)\n    if n == 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Matrix must be non-empty\")\n    # Validate square and numeric entries\n    for row in matrix:\n        if not isinstance(row, list) or len(row) != n:\n            raise ValueError(\"Matrix must be square (N x N)\")\n        for v in row:\n            if not isinstance(v, (int, float)):\n                raise ValueError(\"Matrix elements must be numeric\")\n\n    # dp[r][c] stores the maximum sum to reach cell (r, c)\n    dp = [[0.0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # Initialize the starting cell\n    dp[0][0] = float(matrix[0][0])\n\n    # Fill the first row\n    for c in range(1, n):\n        dp[0][c] = dp[0][c-1] + float(matrix[0][c])\n\n    # Fill the first column\n    for r in range(1, n):\n        dp[r][0] = dp[r-1][0] + float(matrix[r][0])\n\n    # Fill the rest of the dp table\n    for r in range(1, n):\n        for c in range(1, n):\n            dp[r][c] = max(dp[r-1][c], dp[r][c-1]) + float(matrix[r][c])\n\n    # The maximum sum path ends at the bottom-right cell\n    max_total_sum = dp[n-1][n-1]\n\n    # For an N*N matrix, any path from (0,0) to (N-1,N-1) using only right/down moves\n    # has a fixed length of 2*N - 1 cells.\n    path_length = (2 * n) - 1\n\n    # Calculate the maximum average\n    max_average = max_total_sum / path_length\n\n    return max_average"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/728", "solution": "def sum_list(a, b):\n    \"\"\"Computes the element-wise sum of two lists.\n    Assumes input lists are of equal length and contain numeric types.\"\"\"\n    return [x + y for x, y in zip(a, b)]"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/725", "solution": "import re\ndef extract_quotation(text) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Extracts substrings enclosed in double quotation marks from the given text.\n    Handles escaped quotes (\\\") and backslashes (\\\\) within the quoted content.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _unescape_string(s: str) -> str:\n        # Replace escaped backslashes first, then escaped quotes\n        return s.replace(r'\\\\', '\\\\').replace(r'\\\"', '\"')\n\n    # Pattern captures content between double quotes allowing escaped characters inside\n    pattern = re.compile(r'\"((?:\\\\.|[^\"\\\\])*)\"')\n\n    matches = [m.group(1) for m in pattern.finditer(text)]\n    return [_unescape_string(s) for s in matches]"}
