{"task_id": "Mbpp/793", "solution": "def last(arr, target):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the last position (highest index) of an element in a sorted array using binary search.\n    Returns -1 if the target is not found.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = len(arr) - 1\n    result = -1\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if arr[mid] == target:\n            result = mid  # Found a potential last occurrence, try to find a later one\n            low = mid + 1  # Search in the right half\n        elif arr[mid] < target:\n            low = mid + 1  # Target is in the right half\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1  # Target is in the left half\n\n    return result"}
