{"task_id": "Mbpp/799", "solution": "def left_rotate(n: int, d: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates the bits of a 32-bit integer `n` to the left by `d` positions.\n    The rotation is performed within a 32-bit boundary.\n    \"\"\"\n    BIT_WIDTH = 32\n    # Normalize shift (handles large d values)\n    d_normalized = d % BIT_WIDTH\n    if d_normalized == 0:\n        return n & 0xFFFFFFFF\n    # Mask input to 32 bits and perform rotation\n    n_masked = n & 0xFFFFFFFF\n    return ((n_masked << d_normalized) | (n_masked >> (BIT_WIDTH - d_normalized))) & 0xFFFFFFFF"}
