{"task_id": "Mbpp/797", "solution": "def sum_in_range(l: int, r: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of all odd natural numbers within the inclusive range [l, r].\n    Natural numbers are defined as integers greater than or equal to 1.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _sum_of_odds_up_to(n: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Helper to calculate the sum of odd numbers from 1 up to n.\"\"\"\n        if n < 1:\n            return 0\n        # The sum of the first k odd numbers is k*k, where k is (n + 1) // 2.\n        k = (n + 1) // 2\n        return k * k\n\n    # Normalize the range to ensure low <= high.\n    low, high = (l, r) if l <= r else (r, l)\n\n    # Clamp the lower bound to 1, as natural numbers start from 1.\n    NATURAL_MIN = 1\n    low = max(low, NATURAL_MIN)\n\n    # If, after clamping, the effective lower bound is greater than the upper bound,\n    # the range contains no natural numbers, so the sum is 0.\n    if low > high:\n        return 0\n\n    # The sum of odd numbers in [low, high] is calculated by subtracting\n    # the sum of odds up to (low - 1) from the sum of odds up to high.\n    return _sum_of_odds_up_to(high) - _sum_of_odds_up_to(low - 1)"}
